{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Bayesian Optimization + ML Potential Screening of Ethylidyne (\u2013CCH\u2083) Adsorption on Ni\u2013Cu Alloy Surfaces\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook uses **Bayesian Optimization (BoTorch/GPyTorch)** combined with **FAIRChem (formerly Open Catalyst\n",
    "Project) universal ML interatomic potentials (UMA)** to efficiently search for low-energy adsorption\n",
    "configurations of ethylidyne (\u2013CCH\u2083, a coking-precursor surrogate) on Ni\u2013Cu bimetallic alloy surfaces.\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of exhaustively enumerating every Cu-substitution pattern and adsorption site, BO proposes candidate\n",
    "(seed, site-type) configurations, evaluates their adsorption energy with the ML potential (fast surrogate for\n",
    "DFT), and uses a Gaussian Process surrogate model to intelligently pick the next configuration to try \u2014 homing\n",
    "in on low-energy binding motifs in far fewer evaluations than brute-force screening.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Workflow**\n",
    "1. Load a fixed Ni(111)-type slab and randomly substitute a subset of Ni atoms with Cu (seed-controlled).\n",
    "2. Place the adsorbate at a randomly chosen on-top / bridge / hollow site.\n",
    "3. Relax the structure with the FAIRChem UMA potential (LBFGS).\n",
    "4. Check for dissociation/desorption artifacts and reject unphysical outcomes.\n",
    "5. Compute the adsorption energy and feed it back into a BoTorch Gaussian Process.\n",
    "6. Repeat for a fixed budget of BO steps, checkpointing after every step.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Attribution\n",
    "This workflow uses models and tools developed by the Open Catalyst Project / FAIR Chemistry team at Meta AI.\n",
    "If you reuse this notebook, please cite the OC20 dataset/UMA model papers (see FAIRChem docs) and\n",
    "[BoTorch](https://botorch.org/).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Requirements\n",
    "- A free [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/) account with access to the FAIRChem UMA checkpoints\n",
    "  (accept the model license on the model page first).\n",
    "- Input structure files: a slab POSCAR (Ni surface with selective-dynamics tags) and an adsorbate POSCAR.\n",
    "  Small example/placeholder files are provided in `data/`; replace with your own system as needed.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Install dependencies (Colab-friendly)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q fairchem-core ase pymatgen botorch gpytorch scikit-learn pandas\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Hugging Face authentication\n",
    "\n",
